#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Refuse to commit corpus documents.
#
# Arabic financial filings carry per-publisher redistribution terms that this
# repository's licence cannot represent, and git history is permanent — a
# document committed once stays recoverable even after a later deletion. A
# marker redaction does not make a private filing public.
#
# See arabicfinbench/gt/CONVENTIONS.md section 6. CI enforces the same rule, so
# skipping this hook does not get a document merged.
#
# Install: scripts/install-hooks.sh

set -euo pipefail

# Filings. Never tracked, anywhere — there is no legitimate reason for one to
# enter this repository.
DOCS='\.(pdf|docx|jfif)$'

# Scans and page images. A corpus page is indistinguishable from a diagram by
# extension alone, so these are allowed only where documentation assets live.
IMAGES='\.(png|jpe?g)$'
IMAGE_ALLOW='^(docs/|\.github/)'

# Confidential corpora. Here the GROUND TRUTH is the disclosure, not just the
# filing: Test_6.json/.md reproduce the document's text and every table cell, so
# an extension rule does not catch them. Checked on additions AND modifications,
# because a modification to an already-tracked copy publishes it just as well.
# DELETIONS are excluded (diff-filter has no D): removing a confidential file is
# the fix, and a rule that blocks its own remedy is worse than no rule.
# Scores stay publishable; only dataset/<doc>/ content is blocked.
CONFIDENTIAL='^dataset/test_6/'

added=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=A)
touched=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMRT)
staged=$(
    {
        printf '%s\n' "$added" | grep -Ei "$DOCS" || true
        printf '%s\n' "$added" | grep -Ei "$IMAGES" | grep -Ev "$IMAGE_ALLOW" || true
        printf '%s\n' "$touched" | grep -E "$CONFIDENTIAL" || true
    } | grep -v '^$' || true
)

if [ -n "$staged" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: refusing to commit corpus document(s) or confidential ground truth:" >&2
    printf '  %s\n' $staged >&2
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'

Source documents are never committed to this repository. Git history is
permanent, so this cannot be undone by a later deletion.

  - Keep it local: add the directory to .gitignore
  - Publish it: via the Hugging Face dataset, and only with confirmed
    redistribution rights (see arabicfinbench/gt/CONVENTIONS.md section 6)

Override only if you are certain the document is redistributable:
  git commit --no-verify
MSG
    exit 1
fi
